 "An agent decides <0>at run time</0> how many tool rounds it needs. A fixed chain cannot express \"repeat until the model stops asking for tools\".": "",
 "▼ Dive in: <0>Conditional edge</0>": "",
 "A <0>chain</0> is a fixed pipeline (a DAG): data flows one way and each step runs once.": "",
 "An agent must <0>loop</0>: call the model, maybe run tools, call the model again. That needs a <1>cycle</1> and a <2>conditional edge</2> deciding \"again or stop?\".": "",
 "LangGraph models this as a graph of <0>nodes</0> (functions) and <1>edges</1> over a shared <2>state</2>. It is the agent loop from <3>the agent loop</3>, made explicit.": "",
 "The router (conditional edge) is ordinary code: usually \"does the last AI message have tool_calls?\". The LLM only supplies that text; the harness decides what runs next.": "",
 "Because a cycle can run forever, LangGraph enforces a <0/> (a step budget).": "",
