 "Each node reads the state, returns a partial update, and the reducer merges it.": "",
 "Mental model: state is a <0>shared whiteboard</0>; nodes never edit it directly, they hand in updates.": "",
 "▼ Dive in: <0>Try updates</0>": "",
 "The graph has one shared <0>state</0> (a TypedDict or Pydantic model). Each field is a <1>channel</1>.": "",
 "A node returns a <0>partial update</0>, not the whole state. A <1>reducer</1> per channel decides how the update merges in.": "",
 "Without a reducer a channel is <0>overwritten</0>. With <1/> the new messages are <2>appended</2> (or replace a message with the same id).": "",
 "This is why the conversation grows turn by turn: the messages channel is exactly the list that is serialized into one token sequence for the next model call.": "",
 "Reducers also make parallel branches safe: two nodes writing the same channel in one super-step get <0>combined</0>, not clobbered.": "",
