 "▼ Dive in: <0>Try the gate</0>": "",
 "With a <0>checkpointer</0> the graph saves a snapshot of the state after every super-step, keyed by a <1/>. That is the agent's short-term memory and crash recovery.": "",
 "<0/> pauses the graph inside a node and surfaces a payload to a human. Resuming with <1/> continues from the saved checkpoint.": "",
 "Use it for risky tools such as <0/>: the approval decision is a <1>boolean</1> that lives in ordinary code, not in the model.": "",
 "Saved checkpoints can be listed and re-run: \"time travel\" lets you fork from an earlier state and try a different branch.": "",
 "Resuming re-runs the interrupted node from its start, so side effects before <0/> should be idempotent.": "",
 "The in-memory saver is for demos; production uses a database-backed checkpointer.": "",
