 "▼ Dive in: <0>Fan-out demo</0>": "",
 "Multi-agent graphs reuse the same primitives: nodes, edges, state. Each \"agent\" is a node (or a whole subgraph).": "",
 "<0>Supervisor</0>: a router node picks which worker runs next. <1>Handoff</1>: an agent returns <2/> to pass control. <3>Send</3>: fan out one task per item and reduce the results (map-reduce).": "",
 "More agents means more LLM calls and more places to fail. See <0>multi-agent cost</0>.": "",
 "Fan-out writes land in one channel concurrently, so that channel needs a reducer such as <0/>.": "",
 "Start with one agent and a few tools; split only when context or responsibilities genuinely conflict.": "",
